---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Change your OpenAthan speaker’s Wi-Fi, reset a forgotten password, or fix a connection problem while keeping your prayer settings."
>
  <article class="docs wrap">
    <div class="docs-heading">
      <h1>Troubleshooting</h1><p class="lede">
        Change your Wi-Fi or reset a forgotten device password while keeping your prayer settings.
      </p>
    </div><div class="docs-body">
      <p>
        These instructions are for a speaker built with the AtomS3R C126 and Pyramid A167. For
        custom builds, see <a href="/docs/getting-started/#other-hardware">Other hardware</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Connect for USB recovery</h2><ol>
        <li>Unplug the Pyramid’s bottom power cable.</li><li>
          Connect your computer to the Atom’s USB-C with a data cable.
        </li><li>
          Open <a href="/install/">device setup</a> in desktop Chrome or Edge and choose <strong
            >Fix Wi-Fi or password</strong
          >.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>Then choose the change you need:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#change-wifi">Change Wi-Fi</a></li><li>
          <a href="#reset-password">Reset your password</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="change-wifi">Change Wi-Fi</h2>
      <p>
        Choose <strong>Change Wi-Fi</strong>. Select your network or enter its name, enter the Wi-Fi
        password, and select <strong>Save Wi-Fi</strong>. Wait for confirmation before
        disconnecting. If the result is uncertain, <a href="#uncertain-result"
          >check the device before trying again</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h2 id="reset-password">Reset your password</h2>
      <p>
        Choose <strong>Reset device password</strong>, enter a new device password twice, and select <strong
          >Save device password</strong
        >. The old device password is not needed over USB. If no password is set, choose <strong
          >Create device password</strong
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Wait for confirmation before disconnecting. If confirmation is missing, <a
          href="#uncertain-result">check the result</a
        > before attempting another reset.
      </p><p>
        Password recovery signs out existing sessions. It does not reinstall firmware, reset prayer
        settings, or erase playback history.
      </p><p>
        After either change, unplug the Atom’s USB cable and reconnect only the Pyramid’s bottom
        power. Open the device’s settings on the same home network and sign in as <strong
          >admin</strong
        >.
      </p><h2>No device appears</h2><p>
        Check that your cable transfers data and is connected to the Atom’s port. Close other
        browser tabs or serial tools using the device. If you cancelled the browser picker, select
        the connection button again when ready.
      </p><h2>The port is busy or the connection drops</h2><p>
        Close other software using the USB port, reconnect the data cable, and start again. Opening
        or reopening USB has caused temporary Wi-Fi loss on the reference device. Allow time for it
        to reconnect, then select <strong>Refresh status</strong> in USB recovery. This checks the connection
        without changing credentials or reopening USB. Once Wi-Fi is connected and a device password
        is set, select <strong>Open device settings</strong>.
      </p><h2>The Wi-Fi password did not work</h2><p>
        Check the network name and password. Use a 2.4 GHz WPA2/WPA3 personal network, rather than a
        guest sign-in portal or enterprise network. A rejected connection retains the previous saved
        credentials.
      </p><h2 id="uncertain-result">The result is uncertain</h2><p>
        If the connection ends before confirmation, the device may already have saved the change.
        The installer will not automatically send it again. Reconnect and check status before
        another change. A connected status alone may describe the previous network; it does not
        prove an uncertain Wi-Fi change succeeded.
      </p><p>
        For a password change, check the reported password revision and try signing in with the
        password you just chose. If you still cannot sign in after checking the device state, choose <strong
          >Reset device password</strong
        > to set a new one.
      </p><h2>The device reports a storage fault</h2><p>
        Stop making changes and keep the current data. Record the error text without including
        passwords and request help through the <a
          href="https://github.com/OpenAthan-Project/openathan/issues">firmware issue tracker</a
        >. Do not reinstall as a shortcut to repairing credentials.
      </p><h2>The settings page will not open</h2><p>
        Use the device’s exact address, not a generic <code>openathan.local</code>. Try the IP
        fallback from USB setup. Keep your phone on the same home network; guest-network isolation
        can prevent access. An IP address may change after reconnecting, so read it again over USB
        if needed.
      </p><h2>Installation was interrupted</h2><p>
        If USB disconnects during installation, unplug the cable, reload the installer page, then
        reconnect and deliberately start again. If it says the write was verified but setup could
        not reconnect, use USB recovery rather than reinstalling. Do not restore an old full-flash
        backup as routine recovery: it can restore old prayer history.
      </p><p>
        The browser installer does not yet support firmware upgrades on existing devices.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/install/">Open USB recovery</a><a href="/docs/getting-started/"
          >Setup instructions</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
